AWS CloudFormation

AWS CloudFormation AWS ka Infrastructure as Code tool hai jo YAML ya JSON templates se AWS resources automatically create aur manage karta hai.

Terraform

Terraform ek Infrastructure as Code tool hai jo HCL language use karke AWS, Azure aur GCP jaise multiple cloud providers par infrastructure create aur manage karta hai.

Ansible

Ansible ek automation aur configuration management tool hai jo servers par software install, configuration aur application deployment ko automate karta hai.

Ek line me yaad rakho
☁️ CloudFormation = AWS resources banata hai (AWS only)
🌍 Terraform = Har cloud par resources banata hai (Multi-cloud)
⚙️ Ansible = Server ke andar software install aur configure karta hai

>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>

Jenkins

Jenkins ek open-source CI/CD automation tool hai jo code ko automatically build, test aur deploy karta hai.

GitHub Actions

GitHub Actions GitHub ka built-in CI/CD tool hai jo repository ke events (jaise code push) par workflows automatically run karta hai.

GitLab CI/CD

GitLab CI/CD GitLab ka built-in automation tool hai jo build, test aur deployment pipelines ko manage karta hai.

AWS CodePipeline

AWS CodePipeline AWS ki managed CI/CD service hai jo applications ko automatically build, test aur deploy karti hai.

Ek line me yaad rakho
🚀 Jenkins = Sabse popular open-source CI/CD tool.
⚙️ GitHub Actions = GitHub ke andar built-in CI/CD.
🦊 GitLab CI/CD = GitLab ke andar built-in CI/CD.
☁️ AWS CodePipeline = AWS ka managed CI/CD service.

Yaad rakhne ki trick:

Infrastructure banane ke tools: Terraform, CloudFormation
Server configure karne ka tool: Ansible
Code ko build aur deploy karne ke tools: Jenkins, GitHub Actions, GitLab CI/CD, AWS CodePipeline

