Docker

Docker ek containerization platform hai jo application aur uski dependencies ko ek container me package karta hai, jisse application har environment me consistently run karti hai.

Kubernetes

Kubernetes ek container orchestration platform hai jo containers ko deploy, scale, monitor aur manage karta hai.

Amazon ECS

Amazon ECS AWS ki managed container orchestration service hai jo Docker containers ko AWS par run aur manage karne ke liye use hoti hai.

Amazon EKS

Amazon EKS AWS ki managed Kubernetes service hai jo Kubernetes clusters ko AWS par chalane aur manage karna aasaan banati hai.

Ek line me yaad rakho
🐳 Docker = Container banata hai.
☸️ Kubernetes = Containers manage karta hai.
☁️ Amazon ECS = AWS par containers manage karta hai (AWS ka apna solution).
☸️☁️ Amazon EKS = AWS par Kubernetes chalata hai.
Yaad rakhne ki trick
Code
   ↓
Docker (Container)
   ↓
Kubernetes / ECS / EKS (Container Management)
   ↓
AWS Server
   ↓
Users

Short Formula:

Docker = Container
Kubernetes = Container Manager
ECS = AWS Container Manager
EKS = AWS Kubernetes

